A||N||9||Babygirl||Upgrade 4 cyl to v-6?||||3||
Z||000000||Babygirl||09-13-2000||03:53 PM||||I have an '84 SE with a 4 cyl, 4 speed, 2.5l.  Is it worth the time to install a V-6 2.8l?  Is the power really there?  If so, how difficult is it?  My husband wants to swap the engines so that I can go faster.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>~Darcy & Laura<BR>1984 Black SE Fiero||||reg||3
Z||000001||LAMBO||09-13-2000||04:07 PM||||This topic has been discussed very thouroughly in previous posts. Go to the Tech. Discuss. archives and you'll have hours worth of reading related to this subject. <BR>Happy reading! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Babygirl||09-13-2000||10:18 PM||||Thanks!  I forgot about the archives!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>~Darcy & Laura<BR>1984 Black SE Fiero||||reg||6
Z||000003||BroCar 87||09-13-2000||10:38 PM||||Hey BABY, I also have an 84 SE, with a 4 speed. I have looked into this swap, and it doesn't look good. ALL the TROUBLE comes from the fact that the 84 never came with the v-6 option. Thus (hehe, sounding technical here), it has a different cradle.<BR>If you find out any good news, I'd like to here about it... ô¿ô  cya!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NorthFLFieroSIG.jpg">    <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||6
Z||000004||StuGood||09-15-2000||12:54 AM||||The power is really there, with the V6.  So is the torque really there.<P>A friend of mine did a 4-cyl to V6 swap years ago, with very little difficulty.  His method was quite simple - <P>Step 1) Remove 4-cyl Fiero.<BR>Step 2) Replace with V6 Fiero.<P>Warning: Use of this method may have side effects, such as a change in the color of the car.   <P>My friend accomplished his swap shortly after he rode in my 1986 SE V6, to get parts for his black 1984 Fiero, which had broken a head bolt.  Not long afterward he was driving a brand new white 1986.5 (or 1987?) Fiero GT.  Beautiful car.  "I'm blaming <B>you</B> for this!," he told me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<P>The difference between the two cars was like black and white  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.  <P> <P> <P>      <P>||||reg||12
Z||000005||Standard||09-15-2000||02:36 AM||||The wiring in the 84 is completly different than in the other years.  It would probably be easier putting a carbed v-8 in there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I have an 84 and an 86, and after working on the 86 all summer it's hard to retrain my brain to the different set-up...<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 150,000 miles and counting!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif">    <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker||||reg||1
Z||000006||tgowens||09-15-2000||03:26 AM||||Babygirl, there are quite a few modifications that will need to be made to your '84 including the wiring harnesses for both the engine and the vehicle. right now we (Fiero Shop) are upgrading a 4 cyl 2.5l to a 6 cyl 3.4l V-6. In fact, we are doing quite a few 2.8 to 3.4 swaps as well, the 3.4 has a horsepower rating of 185hp which is 50hp better than a stock 2.8l -- there is a noticable horsepower improvement. unless you already have the 2.8l engine i would sugest that, for the investment it would be well worth it to swap the 2.5l with a 3.4.<P>If you have any questions, call either George or me at the Fiero Shop - 1-510-23-FIERO (1-510-233-4376<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/Terry_sig.gif">                     <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A><BR>Gold '87 GT<BR>Blue '87 GT<p>[This message has been edited by tgowens (edited 09-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||tgowens||09-15-2000||03:33 AM||||Brocar87, the cradle is basically the same for the 84-87 - the '88 had a different cradle due to the elimination of the A-frame suspension in favor of the trailing arm suspension. there were a few different cradles for different transmissions but the main point (and i say this in case you ever want to make an engine swap) is that an '84 cradle with a 4 cyl engine installed <I>will</I> support a V-6. -- just trying to help.......<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/Terry_sig.gif">                    <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A><BR>Gold '87 GT<BR>Blue '87 GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||BroCar 87||09-15-2000||11:56 PM||||WOW! thanks Terry. I wish we had more of you knowledgable FIERO guys in the North Florida area!!!<BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NorthFLFieroSIG.jpg">    <BR>87 Coupe "IRON BEAST"<BR>84 SE (project)||||reg||1
Z||000009||henrik||09-20-2000||03:15 PM||||Do it, and you will get a smile on your face that last for a long time....<P>The difference is big. The V6 is stronger, sounds better and looks better. I recently replaced my 4-cyl with a v6. My car is a -85 2m4 SE. I took the engine, gear box, cradle, ECM+wiring harness between Ecm and engine from a -87 GT. You will also need another exhaust system. Pictures at <A HREF="http://www.dtek.chalmers.se/~d99hb" TARGET=_blank>www.dtek.chalmers.se/~d99hb</A>  The page is in swedish for the moment and only works in Internet explorer(some bug), but you can still see the pictures :-)||||reg||1
